comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T10:06:12.838Z",codex-agent,"Verified five unresolved threads: PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6vBuTz and PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6vBuT- require publishing-guard citations; PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6vBuT8 and PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6vBuT_ require implementation versus verification attribution; PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6vBuT5 requires both successful CodeQL workflow and analysis receipts. All valid. Main remains 7d156cd179b1; every delivery commit is in main ancestry. CodeQL main run 39410986052 succeeds and analysis 1987756727 has empty error at the same ancestor bbc33ecb6d6d. Self-review covers all ten closeouts; correct the same citation mismatch in p965, a9iw, 05ub and ht20 too. Preserve every prior history byte. No outside-diff findings in the latest CodeRabbit review."
  "2026-10-22T10:13:30.593Z",codex-agent,"Tracker-only evidence verification complete. All five threads are valid and addressed by seven snapshot corrections: publishing guard (594y and self-review p965), merge-wait implementation versus later test (jjbl), paired CodeQL success and analysis (f4tl), deterministic date artifacts (a9iw), both reusable callers (05ub), and historical certification package/launcher artifacts (ht20). Three other closeouts already cite relevant artifacts. All eleven distinct delivery/verification/analysis commits are in unchanged main 7d156cd179b1 ancestry. Each of seven existing PR history streams preserves every prior byte and appends exactly one event; all ten original changed streams preserve main prefixes. Both evidence fields match intended corrections and existing terminal status remains unchanged. This mainline evidence is the tracker-only substitute for behavioral revert proofs. Linked pm test passes 3/3 ancestry commands; npm ci, changelog generation/check, inventory, snapshot, privacy and whitespace checks pass. pm health --check-only --json exits 0 but reports ok=false for existing host-extension version skew and legacy provenance-domain advisory; no strict-health certification or history repair. No runtime or dist edits, no new closure operations, and no review replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release."
